{"content_hash": "24a9402769976740", "version_id": 247, "article_id": 25, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "米国とレバノン、シリアの将軍を守っているとBBCが報道", "title_zh": "BBC爆料：美国和黎巴嫩在保护一名叙利亚将军", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c81dldewl5gwo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/6350/live/ef6a77a0-c1a6-11f1-a64c-550be9e3c66b.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 534, "reading_minutes": 1.7, "lead": "シリアの元将軍が、米国とレバノンに守られています。BBCが調べました。この将軍は、アメリカ人の記者が行方不明になった事件に関係しています。", "lead_zh": "一名叙利亚前将军受到美国和黎巴嫩的保护。BBC进行了调查。这名将军与一名美国记者失踪案有关。", "preview": "BBCの調査によると、シリアの元将軍バッサム・アル＝ハッサンは、米国とレバノンに守られています。彼はシリアの化学兵器の計画を担当し、元大統領バシャール・アル＝アサドの顧問でした。アサド政権が2024年に倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。", "preview_zh": "据BBC调查，叙利亚前将军巴萨姆·哈桑受到美国和黎巴嫩的保护。他曾负责叙利亚的化学武器计划，是前总统巴沙尔·阿萨德的顾问。2024年阿萨德政权倒台后，他留在黎巴嫩。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 237, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/audio/25/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 110.825, "size_bytes": 668736, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 350, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/data/versions/247.json", "paragraphs": ["BBCの調査によると、シリアの元将軍バッサム・アル＝ハッサンは、米国とレバノンに守られています。彼はシリアの化学兵器の計画を担当し、元大統領バシャール・アル＝アサドの顧問でした。アサド政権が2024年に倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。", "米国とレバノンの当局は、ハッサンがレバノンにいることを認めています。理由は、彼が2012年にシリアでアメリカ人記者オースティン・タイスが連れ去られた事件について、情報を出すと言ったからです。FBIもこの取り決めに関わっています。", "シリアの新しい政府は、ハッサンを裁判のために返してほしいと言っています。しかし、米国は彼をレバノンに置きたいと考えています。シリア政府は、自分たちにはできることが少ないと言っています。", "タイスの家族の代表フィル・エルウッドさんは、BBCにこう言いました。「アメリカの税金で、化学兵器を使った人を楽に暮らさせるのは、とてもひどいことです。彼は戦争犯罪人です。裁判を受けるべきです。」", "BBCは、ハッサンがFBIとCIA、レバノンの治安当局と会った記録を見ました。その記録では、ハッサンはタイス事件の情報と引き換えに、レバノンでの居住と保護、生活の支援をもらうと書かれていました。", "ハッサンは去年、タイスはアサドの命令で殺されたと言いました。しかし、彼の話には疑問の声もあります。彼が言った場所を捜索しましたが、何も見つかりませんでした。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["据BBC调查，叙利亚前将军巴萨姆·哈桑受到美国和黎巴嫩的保护。他曾负责叙利亚的化学武器计划，是前总统巴沙尔·阿萨德的顾问。2024年阿萨德政权倒台后，他留在黎巴嫩。", "美国和黎巴嫩当局承认哈桑留在黎巴嫩。原因是他表示愿意提供2012年美国记者奥斯汀·泰斯在叙利亚被绑架事件的信息。FBI也参与了这一安排。", "叙利亚新政府表示希望哈桑回国接受审判。但美国希望他留在黎巴嫩。叙利亚政府表示他们对此无能为力。", "泰斯家人的代表菲尔·埃尔伍德对BBC说：“用美国纳税人的钱让一个使用化学武器的人过舒适生活，这太恶劣了。他是战争罪犯，应该接受审判。”", "BBC看到了哈桑与FBI、CIA以及黎巴嫩安全官员会面的记录。记录显示，哈桑以提供泰斯事件的信息换取在黎巴嫩的居留、保护和生计支持。", "哈桑去年说，泰斯是按照阿萨德的命令被处死的。但有人对他的说法表示怀疑。他提供的地点被搜查过，但什么也没找到。"], "body": "BBCの調査によると、シリアの元将軍バッサム・アル＝ハッサンは、米国とレバノンに守られています。彼はシリアの化学兵器の計画を担当し、元大統領バシャール・アル＝アサドの顧問でした。アサド政権が2024年に倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。\n\n米国とレバノンの当局は、ハッサンがレバノンにいることを認めています。理由は、彼が2012年にシリアでアメリカ人記者オースティン・タイスが連れ去られた事件について、情報を出すと言ったからです。FBIもこの取り決めに関わっています。\n\nシリアの新しい政府は、ハッサンを裁判のために返してほしいと言っています。しかし、米国は彼をレバノンに置きたいと考えています。シリア政府は、自分たちにはできることが少ないと言っています。\n\nタイスの家族の代表フィル・エルウッドさんは、BBCにこう言いました。「アメリカの税金で、化学兵器を使った人を楽に暮らさせるのは、とてもひどいことです。彼は戦争犯罪人です。裁判を受けるべきです。」\n\nBBCは、ハッサンがFBIとCIA、レバノンの治安当局と会った記録を見ました。その記録では、ハッサンはタイス事件の情報と引き換えに、レバノンでの居住と保護、生活の支援をもらうと書かれていました。\n\nハッサンは去年、タイスはアサドの命令で殺されたと言いました。しかし、彼の話には疑問の声もあります。彼が言った場所を捜索しましたが、何も見つかりませんでした。", "body_zh": "据BBC调查，叙利亚前将军巴萨姆·哈桑受到美国和黎巴嫩的保护。他曾负责叙利亚的化学武器计划，是前总统巴沙尔·阿萨德的顾问。2024年阿萨德政权倒台后，他留在黎巴嫩。\n\n美国和黎巴嫩当局承认哈桑留在黎巴嫩。原因是他表示愿意提供2012年美国记者奥斯汀·泰斯在叙利亚被绑架事件的信息。FBI也参与了这一安排。\n\n叙利亚新政府表示希望哈桑回国接受审判。但美国希望他留在黎巴嫩。叙利亚政府表示他们对此无能为力。\n\n泰斯家人的代表菲尔·埃尔伍德对BBC说：“用美国纳税人的钱让一个使用化学武器的人过舒适生活，这太恶劣了。他是战争罪犯，应该接受审判。”\n\nBBC看到了哈桑与FBI、CIA以及黎巴嫩安全官员会面的记录。记录显示，哈桑以提供泰斯事件的信息换取在黎巴嫩的居留、保护和生计支持。\n\n哈桑去年说，泰斯是按照阿萨德的命令被处死的。但有人对他的说法表示怀疑。他提供的地点被搜查过，但什么也没找到。", "text": "BBCの調査によると、シリアの元将軍バッサム・アル＝ハッサンは、米国とレバノンに守られています。彼はシリアの化学兵器の計画を担当し、元大統領バシャール・アル＝アサドの顧問でした。アサド政権が2024年に倒れた後、彼はレバノンにいます。 米国とレバノンの当局は、ハッサンがレバノンにいることを認めています。理由は、彼が2012年にシリアでアメリカ人記者オースティン・タイスが連れ去られた事件について、情報を出すと言ったからです。FBIもこの取り決めに関わっています。 シリアの新しい政府は、ハッサンを裁判のために返してほしいと言っています。しかし、米国は彼をレバノンに置きたいと考えています。シリア政府は、自分たちにはできることが少ないと言っています。 タイスの家族の代表フィル・エルウッドさんは、BBCにこう言いました。「アメリカの税金で、化学兵器を使った人を楽に暮らさせるのは、とてもひどいことです。彼は戦争犯罪人です。裁判を受けるべきです。」 BBCは、ハッサンがFBIとCIA、レバノンの治安当局と会った記録を見ました。その記録では、ハッサンはタイス事件の情報と引き換えに、レバノンでの居住と保護、生活の支援をもらうと書かれていました。 ハッサンは去年、タイスはアサドの命令で殺されたと言いました。しかし、彼の話には疑問の声もあります。彼が言った場所を捜索しましたが、何も見つかりませんでした。", "vocab": [{"word": "将軍", "pos": "noun", "zh": "将军", "note": ""}, {"word": "守る", "pos": "verb", "zh": "保护；守卫", "note": "五段动词，这里用被动形「守られている」"}, {"word": "調査", "pos": "noun", "zh": "调查", "note": "する动词：調査する"}, {"word": "化学兵器", "pos": "noun", "zh": "化学武器", "note": ""}, {"word": "大統領", "pos": "noun", "zh": "总统", "note": ""}, {"word": "政権", "pos": "noun", "zh": "政权", "note": ""}, {"word": "記者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "记者", "note": ""}, {"word": "裁判", "pos": "noun", "zh": "审判；法庭", "note": ""}, {"word": "税金", "pos": "noun", "zh": "税金", "note": ""}, {"word": "情報", "pos": "noun", "zh": "情报；信息", "note": ""}], "title_original": "US and Lebanon protecting wanted Syrian general, BBC finds", "summary_original": "Bassam al-Hassan, linked to reporter Austin Tice's abduction, is being sheltered in return for information.", "body_original": "US and Lebanon protecting wanted Syrian general, BBC finds\nBy\nSara Obeidat\nand\nJosh Baker\nPublished\n4 hours ago\nA former Syrian general wanted for\ncrimes against humanity\n,\nexternal\nis being bankrolled and protected by the US and Lebanese authorities, a BBC News investigation has found.\nBassam al-Hassan, who oversaw Syria's chemical weapons programme and was a senior adviser to former President Bashar al-Assad, is being harboured in Lebanon following the Assad regime's collapse in 2024.\nAn investigation by the BBC and the US broadcaster NPR has discovered that Hassan has been allowed to remain there under an arrangement involving the FBI, and other US and Lebanese authorities. This is because of his willingness to provide information about the abduction of American journalist Austin Tice in Syria in 2012, as well as additional intelligence, we have been told.\nLast month the BBC revealed Tice's abduction had been a\nplanned operation\n, with Hassan in the chain of command.\nOfficials from two different branches of Syria's new government have told the BBC they want Hassan returned to face trial, but that US authorities want him kept in Lebanon, and they say there is little Damascus can do about this.\nWe asked the FBI, the CIA and Lebanon's General Directorate of General Security to comment on our findings. Only the FBI responded, declining to comment and instead directing us to a past statement that said its focus remained on establishing the facts around the Tice case and securing his return.\nIn response to our findings, Phil Elwood, spokesperson for the Tice family said: \"If what you are saying is true, the fact that our tax dollars are being used to furnish a comfortable life for someone associated with the use of chemical weapons on Syrian civilians, who claims to have had Austin Tice executed, is offensive.\n\"This is nothing less than aiding and abetting the escape of a wanted war criminal. The Syrians deserve justice and he should be returned to stand trial.\"\nWhere is Austin Tice?\nJosh Baker enters a dangerous world of fear, greed and betrayal as he uncovers what happened in one of the biggest missing-person cases of our time - the abduction of Austin Tice.\nListen on Sounds\nSeries Three of I'm Not A Monster Presents\nAs part of a years-long investigation featured in the new\nBBC podcast: Where is Austin Tice?\nthe BBC has reviewed a detailed record of a meeting between Hassan, FBI and CIA representatives, and Lebanese security officials, where Tice's case is discussed.\nIn it, Hassan is offered \"residency\", \"protection\" and help securing his \"living needs\" in return for information, primarily about Tice.\nSources with knowledge of the arrangement confirmed this was the case, and described to us how Hassan receives money from the US authorities through an intermediary, making it harder to trace. Hassan is sanctioned by the US government.\nYet people connected to the Tice investigation say they have seen little evidence it has significantly advanced since Hassan began providing information as part of this agreement. The deal is believed to have been struck in the spring of 2025.\nSources with knowledge of the investigation have expressed concerns that Hassan's arrangement with the US could continue indefinitely, at significant expense but with little gain.\nHassan is not the only Syrian regime official whose connection to the Tice case has seemingly afforded him financial payments or assistance for living abroad.\nOne former regime member said he had received money from the FBI multiple times in exchange for his co-operation on Tice's case. It was \"not in his interest to share all the information all at once,\" he told the BBC, \"in order to be able to drag out how long he can continue to receive payments from them [the US authorities]\".\nAnother former regime member connected to the Tice case claimed he was living in Lebanon under the \"patronage\" of the US authorities, citing this as the reason he could not speak to us about Tice.\nThe BBC spoke to a former senior Lebanese intelligence official who confirmed that Lebanese intelligence does have arrangements with the Americans, and that these types of payments have and do take place when both agencies have overlap in cases, but said he had no knowledge of payments involving the Tice case.\nFollowing the fall of the Assad regime in early December 2024, Hassan is believed to have initially escaped to Iran.\nA Syrian businessman, with strong connections to both the former regime and the Lebanese authorities, told the BBC that negotiations had then taken place - involving the US, Lebanon, and Iran - to bring Hassan to Lebanon.\nThe businessman, who asked to remain anonymous, said Hassan was valuable, not only because of what he is believed to know about Tice, but because of his knowledge of Syria's chemical weapons programme and its military relationship with Iran - secrets that US intelligence was allegedly interested in.\nHassan told US investigators last year that Tice\nhad been executed\non former President Assad's orders, but several people with knowledge of the investigation have questioned the details of his account. Hassan has provided a potential location for Tice's remains, but when the site was searched, nothing was found - according to multiple sources familiar with the dig - casting doubt on the validity of some of Hassan's information.\nThere are questions, however, over how thoroughly the site was searched. Two sources who said they had intimate knowledge of the operation told the BBC that US authorities stopped digging before the search had been completed, possibly because of security concerns.\nWhen the BBC managed to reach Hassan by phone last year to ask for an interview, he directed us to seek permission for him to speak from the FBI and CIA at the US embassy in Beirut.\nOur investigation has found that other Syrian officials connected to the Tice case have also apparently found refuge abroad.\nThey include Mohammad Makhlouf, who reported to Hassan in Syria and was connected to Tice's detention - now believed to be residing in Lebanon. And Sakr Rustom, Hassan's nephew who was involved in Tice's abduction, now believed to be moving between the UAE and Lebanon. When the BBC attempted to speak to Rustom about Tice's case, he said he \"preferred to focus on matters of the future\".\nGhassan Nassour, a former general in Syria's Republican Guard, is said by former members of the National Defence Forces to have presided over the jail Tice was held in, and is believed to be living in the UAE with his family, we have been told.\nRelated topics\nSyria\nUS government\nUnited States\nFBI\nCIA\nSyrian civil war\nBashar al-Assad", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T09:37:52.374921+00:00", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "BBC", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.8, "sm": 125, "em": 800, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.812, "e": 0.912, "sm": 812, "em": 912, "cs": 3, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "調査", "s": 0.925, "e": 1.312, "sm": 925, "em": 1312, "cs": 4, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, 